+# Todo due dates implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional due dates and consistent overdue information to the JSON API and list page for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** Keep the singleton `TodoStore` shared by the API and Blazor page. Represent dates with nullable `DateOnly`; compute overdue state from the current UTC day. Distinguish omitted PATCH dates from explicit null using a request property's setter, without changing title/done patch behavior.
+
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, System.Text.Json, xUnit, WebApplicationFactory, Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** Agreed in the conversation for ticket #1: optional `dueDate` formatted `YYYY-MM-DD`; create and update via API; omitted PATCH field preserves the date and null clears it; responses include `dueDate` and `isOverdue`; display dates and a clear overdue marker in the list. A todo is overdue exactly when unfinished and its due date precedes today in UTC. Undated todos are never overdue. The agent runs end-to-end browser checks.
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- TDD: write a failing test in `tests/` first.
+- Validation errors are `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`, thrown by `TodoStore`; `Program.cs` maps them to HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}`.
+- Every UI element tests rely on carries a `data-testid` attribute; give new elements one too.
+- The page uses `TodoStore` directly; it never calls the app's own HTTP API.
+- Branch: `1_faelligkeitsdatum_todos`; base: `main`; finish with a draft PR, leaving the issue open in `status:review`.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- Empty strings, timestamps, impossible dates, numbers and objects must return HTTP 400 with an `error` field, without changing stored data.
+- Title-only, done-only and empty patches must preserve an existing date; explicit null clears it.
+- Today is never overdue; dates are compared against UTC rather than server-local time.
+- Completing and reopening an overdue todo must immediately change its computed status in API responses and on a freshly loaded page.
+- Existing clients can still omit the date; missing todo IDs retain HTTP 404 behavior.
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Date model, store and API
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`, and `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`. Change `src/DemoTodo/Program.cs` only if request binding requires it.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: existing `TodoStore.Add(NewTodo)`, `Update(int, TodoPatch)`, `Get(int)` and `List()`.
+- Produces: `Todo.DueDate: DateOnly?`, `Todo.IsOverdue: bool`, optional `NewTodo.DueDate`, and `TodoPatch.DueDate` with presence tracking. Preserve existing constructors using optional parameters; JSON is camel case.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write failing store and API tests.** Assert omitted/null create dates are null and not overdue; valid dates round-trip through POST, GET and list. Test yesterday/today/tomorrow with done true/false. Test setting/replacing/clearing a date and preservation for title-only, done-only and empty patches. Test reopening. Assert malformed dates on POST/PATCH return 400 JSON errors and leave data intact; valid leap days work; missing IDs return 404.
+- [x] **Step 2: Verify RED.** Run `dotnet test --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~TodoStoreTests|FullyQualifiedName~TodoApiTests'`. Expected: new assertions fail because date fields/overdue behavior do not exist (or compilation identifies those missing interfaces).
+- [x] **Step 3: Implement the date contract.** Extend the records using nullable `DateOnly` and calculate `IsOverdue` as `!Done && DueDate is { } date && date < DateOnly.FromDateTime(DateTime.UtcNow)`. Use an init setter and JSON-ignored presence flag for patch dates; preserve the date when absent and apply null when present. Use existing JSON binding and error middleware.
+- [x] **Step 4: Verify GREEN.** Run `dotnet test`. Expected: all store/API tests pass; update the existing exact JSON expectation to include the agreed response fields.
+- [x] **Step 5: Commit.** Stage the model and tests; commit `feat: add optional todo due dates and overdue API status`.
+
+### Task 2: List display and browser verification
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor`; create `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoPageTests.cs`. Add scoped page CSS only if necessary.
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Consumes: Task 1's `Todo.DueDate` and `Todo.IsOverdue`, from `TodoStore.List()`.
+- Produces: semantic `<time>` with `data-testid="todo-due-date"` and ISO `datetime`; visible `Überfällig` text with `data-testid="todo-overdue"` for overdue todos only. Preserve existing list/title test IDs.
+
+- [x] **Step 1: Write failing page tests.** Seed each test app's store through its API. Assert ISO dates render in `<time>`, overdue todos have the marker, and today/future/done/undated todos do not. Verify completing or clearing the date removes the marker on a fresh page load.
+- [x] **Step 2: Verify RED.** Run `dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~TodoPageTests`. Expected: missing date/overdue markup assertions fail.
+- [x] **Step 3: Implement the page display.** Render the optional date in ISO format and an accessible text badge for `todo.IsOverdue`; give new date and badge elements their specified test IDs.
+- [x] **Step 4: Verify GREEN.** Run `dotnet test`. Expected: all tests pass.
+- [x] **Step 5: Commit.** Commit `feat: show todo due dates and overdue markers`.
+- [x] **Step 6: Run browser end to end.** Start the app using `AGENTS.md`; wait for `/health`. Use Playwright MCP to create yesterday/today/future/undated/done cases through API requests, then load `/` and wait for the Blazor circuit. Assert dates/markers per row. Change dates, clear a date, complete and reopen a todo, reload and verify each transition. Check malformed requests and omission preservation. Capture a screenshot outside the repository and shut the app down.
+- [x] **Step 7: Review and close out.** Obtain a fresh code review, address important findings with RED→GREEN tests, run `dotnet test`, push, create a `WIP:` PR using `tea`, post implementation and cost summaries, and move ticket #1 to review.
+
+## Verification evidence
+
+- Automated suite: `dotnet test` — 48 passed, 0 failed.
+- Playwright MCP: 85 functional assertions plus 30 display assertions passed against the running app on 2026-10-21 UTC, covering yesterday/today/tomorrow, undated/completed todos, date replacement/clearing, omission preservation, completion/reopening, and malformed date rejection. Each page load waited for the Blazor circuit.
+- Browser console: no warnings or errors. Screenshot: `/tmp/todo-ticket-1-e2e.png` (outside the repository). App stopped after testing.
+- Independent whole-branch review: no critical, important or minor findings. Reviewer independently ran `TZ=Pacific/Honolulu dotnet test --no-restore`: 48 passed; `git diff --check` passed.
+- Close-out: draft PR http://gitea:3000/adw/demo-todo/pulls/2 opened against `main`; implementation and cost summaries posted to ticket #1; ticket remains open with `status:review`.
